e: 1","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5905821075/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5906055946","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-5906055946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":5906055946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYAdDCg","user":{"login":"bodyfing","id":143592076,"node_id":"U_kgDOCI8KjA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143592076?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing","html_url":"https://github.com/bodyfing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bodyfing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T07:08:37Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T07:08:37Z","body":"Thanks, bro. It recovered after running these commands:\ncodex app-server daemon stop\ncodex app-server daemon update --from-cli\ncodex app-server daemon start","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5906055946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5916618476","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-5916618476","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":5916618476,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYKhu7A","user":{"login":"OrcaWin","id":293788423,"node_id":"U_kgDOEYLbBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/293788423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin","html_url":"https://github.com/OrcaWin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OrcaWin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T17:47:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T17:47:25Z","body":"I reproduced this on Windows 11 x64 with Codex CLI `0.159.2` installed via npm and the Orca-managed app-server runtime.\n\nThe CLI and daemon initially reported different versions: CLI `0.159.2`, managed daemon/app-server `0.157.1`. The normal update path failed:\n\n```powershell\ncodex app-server daemon stop\ncodex app-server daemon update\n```\n\n```text\nError: standalone Codex updater exited with status exit code: 1\n```\n\nThe updater stderr log was empty, so there was no actionable diagnostic.\n\nThe explicit CLI-copy update succeeded:\n\n```powershell\ncodex app-server daemon update --from-cli --yes\ncodex app-server daemon restart\ncodex app-server daemon version\n```\n\nThe final version check reported matching versions:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"running\",\n  \"managedCodexVersion\": \"0.159.2\",\n  \"cliVersion\": \"0.159.2\",\n  \"appServerVersion\": \"0.159.2\"\n}\n```\n\nThis suggests the production updater path is failing on Windows, while copying the CLI package works. The CLI also does not automatically resolve the version mismatch after its own upgrade. A clearer diagnostic or automatic synchronization would help. The `--from-cli` path pins the daemon package, so users also need to understand how to return to production updates.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5916618476/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5925374314","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-5925374314","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":5925374314,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYS4Jag","user":{"login":"vladzdev","id":374240,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NDI0MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/374240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev","html_url":"https://github.com/vladzdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vladzdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T05:31:03Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T05:31:03Z","body":"Having the CLI report one version while the daemon is actually running another is the sort of thing that makes debugging needlessly expensive. A single \"effective runtime version\" in the diagnostics would probably save a lot of time.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5925374314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5944397698","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-5944397698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":5944397698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYlBPgg","user":{"login":"ochiai-PCKK","id":191941698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3DMQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191941698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK","html_url":"https://github.com/ochiai-PCKK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ochiai-PCKK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T02:19:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T02:19:56Z","body":"Additional confirmed report on Windows 11 Enterprise x64 (build 26100), with Codex CLI installed through mise's `npm:@openai/codex` backend.\n\nThe active mise installation was **0.160.0**, but the managed daemon still launched **0.157.1** from its separate package directory. Stopping the old daemon was insufficient: after another invocation without `--no-daemon`, the old daemon started again.\n\nObserved state before recovery (user-specific paths redacted):\n\n```text\nActive CLI:\n  <mise-installs>/npm-openai-codex/0.160.0/.../bin/codex.exe\n\nManaged daemon processes:\n  <CODEX_HOME>/packages/app-server-daemon/releases/0.157.1-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc/bin/codex.exe\n    app-server --listen unix:// --managed-daemon\n  same executable:\n    app-server daemon pid-update-loop\n\n<CODEX_HOME>/packages/app-server-daemon/current\n  junction -> releases/0.157.1-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc\n\n<CODEX_HOME>/packages/app-server-daemon/auto-update-version\n  contents: 0.157.1-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc\n```\n\nThe current session using `resume --no-daemon` ran the mise-installed 0.160.0 executable, independently of the old managed daemon. This was therefore a stale installed daemon package/reference, not merely an old process surviving an update.\n\nRecovery succeeded after stopping the old daemon and running the **0.160.0 CLI executable** with:\n\n```text\ncodex app-server daemon update --from-cli --yes\n```\n\nThe command returned `status: updated`, `installedVersion: 0.160.0`, and `runningVersion: null`. The `current` junction then pointed to a new `releases/local-...-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` package, whose executable reported `codex-cli 0.160.0`.\n\nNote that this workaround explicitly pins the copied CLI package; it does not establish automatic synchronization with future mise updates. We have not determined why the daemon package remained on 0.157.1, whether a daemon update was attempted or failed, or whether it had previously been explicitly pinned. The exact original upgrade command was not captured.\n\nPlease include external package-manager upgrades such as mise/npm in the proposed version-mismatch detection and recovery flow. Checking only the CLI installation/version can give users the impression that they are running the updated version while normal daemon-backed launches still use the old package.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5944397698/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5947703643","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-5947703643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":5947703643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYoLBWw","user":{"login":"cmp0xff","id":5564164,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NjQxNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5564164?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff","html_url":"https://github.com/cmp0xff","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cmp0xff/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:51:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T07:51:25Z","body":"Additional report on macOS with Codex CLI installed through Homebrew:\n\n- CLI version: `0.160.0`\n- Background service version: `0.159.2`\n- Warning: “A background Codex service is running v0.159.2, older than your Codex CLI v0.160.0”\n\nThe warning provided no recovery instruction. Running `codex app-server daemon update --from-cli` resolved it. No functional failure was observed; the concern is the unexplained warning and having to discover the recovery command.\n\nPlease include the applicable recovery command in the warning, explaining that `--from-cli` pins the daemon package to the selected CLI build and that updating may interrupt active work.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5947703643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5951820015","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-5951820015","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":5951820015,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYsGQ7w","user":{"login":"NihaoShao","id":50469399,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDY5Mzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50469399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao","html_url":"https://github.com/NihaoShao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NihaoShao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T11:55:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T11:55:24Z","body":"I just hit the same managed app-server version skew on the official standalone installation, and in my case it appears to have had a user-visible effect on model availability.\n\nAfter upgrading Codex CLI, I had:\n\n```text\ncliVersion:          0.160.0\nmanagedCodexVersion: 0.158.0\nappServerVersion:    0.158.0\n```\n\nThe managed daemon's `current` binary itself still reported:\n\n```text\ncodex-cli 0.158.0\n```\n\nSo restarting the daemon alone did not help — it simply restarted the stale 0.158.0 managed package.\n\nAt the same time, GPT-6.1 Sol was already available in Codex Desktop for the same ChatGPT Plus account, but was unavailable in Codex CLI. After cleaning/reinitializing the stale local Codex/app-server state and signing in again through the official ChatGPT flow, Sol immediately became available in the CLI.\n\nI filed #50287 with the full Sol-specific reproduction/workaround.\n\nThis makes automatic version alignment particularly important: users can see a fully updated `codex --version` and assume they are testing the current release, while the managed app-server is still executing older code. In some cases that may affect more than daemon-specific bug fixes — it may also affect model discovery/filtering or other runtime behavior.\n\nIt would be helpful if a CLI upgrade automatically updated/restarted the managed daemon, or at minimum emitted a prominent warning whenever:\n\n```text\ncliVersion != managedCodexVersion\n```\n\nor\n\n```text\ncliVersion != appServerVersion\n```\n\nespecially since this mismatch is not obvious from `codex --version` alone.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5951820015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/6036794294","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49418#issuecomment-6036794294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49418","id":6036794294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABZ9Irtg","user":{"login":"snowyukitty","id":270071858,"node_id":"U_kgDOEBj4Mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270071858?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty","html_url":"https://github.com/snowyukitty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowyukitty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-07T11:17:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T11:17:45Z","body":"A concrete failure mode from this gap, in case it helps prioritise. With the standalone CLI on `0.160.1` and the managed daemon still on `0.158.0`, turns run by the daemon with the newest configured model failed with:\n\n```\n400 ... The 'gpt-6.1-sol' model is not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account.\n```\n\nThe model list is fetched per `client_version`, so the stale daemon never sees newer models. To the user this looks like an account entitlement problem. After the daemon was updated, the same model worked on the same account.\n\nIn my case the daemon hadn't updated because its updater runs the served `install.ps1` with output discarded. Details and a workaround are in #27117.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/6036794294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]